From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:28:05 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] safetylib: implement the safety checker for ARMv8-A

jasmin-checksafety rejected every ARMv8-A program with "the safety
checker is not implemented for ARMv8-A". Instantiate the analysis with
the abstraction ARMv7-M and RISC-V already use: the outputs of
architecture-specific operators are unknown, and no comparison or
conditional-instruction heuristic is applied. Memory and array accesses,
initialization and alignment are checked by the generic analysis.

The safety test runner now also analyzes the common tests on ARMv8-A.
New success/armv8a and fail/armv8a tests cover 64-bit memory and array
accesses, alignment, the initialization of the memory an LDP reads, and
the result of an ARMv8-A operator used as an index with and without a
mask.
